WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.470
- [Narrator] These days you can learn

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.516
practically anything from the internet.

00:00:03.516 --> 00:00:04.349
(xylophone chimes)

00:00:04.349 --> 00:00:06.000
So the concept of being an apprentice

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:08.900
craftsman may seem a little old school.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:11.520
But here in the countryside
of Kōchi, Japan,

00:00:11.520 --> 00:00:13.540
there is a small blacksmith workshop,

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.280
where the apprenticeship style of learning

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.330
has not completely disappeared.

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:19.913
(upbeat music)

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:27.180
These blades are called
Nata, and they are used

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:29.190
by professional woodcutters here in Kōchi,

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.900
which is a heavily forested
region of the country.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.993
They are the tool chiefly
made by this master craftsman.

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.980
But three years ago,
after nearly a lifetime

00:01:00.980 --> 00:01:04.433
of working alone, Matsumura
was joined by a young man.

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:12.880
(laughing)

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.437
When he learned about
Matsumura, Kikuchi left

00:01:14.437 --> 00:01:17.230
his manufacturing job in the city

00:01:17.230 --> 00:01:19.270
and approached the aging master

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:22.293
who was hesitant to take on
the young man as an apprentice.

00:01:44.570 --> 00:01:46.680
And for Kikuchi, it's
not only about learning

00:01:46.680 --> 00:01:50.013
from his master, but learning
how to think like his master.

00:02:33.571 --> 00:02:36.154
(upbeat music)

